# ntdll: Fix target unwinding to nested exception handlers on x86-64.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12419 state=opened
# The search pass selects an __except handler; the unwind pass must clean up
only scopes exited on the way to it. An enclosing __finally in the same frame
should not run prematurely.

In msvcrt/handler4.c, call_catch_block4() uses this nesting for C++ rethrows.
The outer __finally runs before the inner __except sets ctx.rethrow, then
runs again when that handler rethrows the original exception. This double
cleanup caused the NULL dereference observed in __CxxUnregisterExceptionObject()
while unlinking an already removed frame.

During EXCEPTION_TARGET_UNWIND, stop scanning at the __except entry whose
ImageBase + JumpTarget matches TargetIp. Enclosing __finally handlers must
be preserved until their scopes are actually exited.

Example (pseudocode): one stack frame F with nested lexical scopes A and B.

    nested() {                         /* frame F */
        __try {                        /* scope A */
            __try {                    /* scope B */
                raise(E);
            } __except (accept(E)) {   /* handler H, still inside A */
                rethrow(E);            /* to a handler in the caller */
            }
        } __finally {
            cleanup();
        }
    }

An illustrative scope table for F could contain the following records.
The filter and cleanup routines are at RVAs 0x300 and 0x400 respectively.

    Scope       BeginAddress  EndAddress  HandlerAddress  JumpTarget
    B           0x100         0x180       0x300           0x200
    A[0]        0x100         0x180       0x400           0
    A[1]        0x200         0x240       0x400           0

A[0] and A[1] describe two code ranges of the same lexical scope A;
they are not separate stack frames.

When E selects handler H, suppose ScopeIndex = 0, ControlPc = base + 0x140
and TargetIp = base + 0x200, where base is ImageBase. The unwind flags
include EXCEPTION_UNWINDING and EXCEPTION_TARGET_UNWIND. Skipping B reaches
A[0], whose range excludes TargetIp, so cleanup runs too 
--- dlls/ntdll/unwind.c
+++ dlls/ntdll/unwind.c
@@ -2265,7 +2265,18 @@ EXCEPTION_DISPOSITION WINAPI __C_specific_handler( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, void *
         {
             if (pc < base + table->ScopeRecord[i].BeginAddress) continue;
             if (pc >= base + table->ScopeRecord[i].EndAddress) continue;
-            if (table->ScopeRecord[i].JumpTarget) continue;
+            /* Stop at the selected __except scope during target unwind.
+             * Its landing pad may lie outside an enclosing __finally's
+             * recorded range even though that scope has not been exited.
+             */
+            if (table->ScopeRecord[i].JumpTarget)
+            {
+                if ((rec->ExceptionFlags & EXCEPTION_TARGET_UNWIND) &&
+                    dispatch->TargetIp ==
+                      base + table->ScopeRecord[i].JumpTarget)
+                    break;
+                continue;
+            }
 
             if (rec->ExceptionFlags & EXCEPTION_TARGET_UNWIND &&
                 dispatch->TargetIp >= base + table->ScopeRecord[i].BeginAddress &&

